  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mini Niko Kazi Youth Employment Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The MNK Internship Programme is based on a private sector demand led approach. It tackles information failures in the labour market. It reduces recruitment risks and transaction costs by matching the supply and demand for skilled employment using economies of scale. The primary beneficiaries of the Mimi Niko Kazi Youth Employment Programme will include young women and men between the ages of 18 and 25. Most of them will have received some post-secondary education, either technical vocational educational training (TVET) or other forms of tertiary education.</narrative>
  </description>
